.TH NOTIFY-CENTER-COLLECTOR 1 "2026-10-27" "notify-center" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
notify-center-collector \- drain Notification Center spool files into a local history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B notify-center-collector
.RB [ \-\-once ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-\-poll " seconds" ]
.RB [ \-\-data-dir " directory" ]
.RB [ \-\-config " file" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B notify-center-collector
turns the JSON notification records written by the Notification Center
Cinnamon applet into a local SQLite history. It also maintains
.I status.json
so the applet can show an unread count without reading SQLite itself.
.PP
The collector normally runs at login from the
.B notify-center-collector.service
systemd user unit, started by an XDG autostart helper. It requires only the
Python standard library.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-once
Drain the spool once and exit. Useful for testing and for creating the
database when the service has never run.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log every spool file that is processed.
.TP
.BI \-\-poll " seconds"
Seconds between spool scans. Defaults to 2.
.TP
.BI \-\-data-dir " directory"
Use a different data directory instead of
.IR ~/.local/share/notify-center .
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Use a different configuration file instead of
.IR ~/.config/notify-center/config.json .
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/notify-center/notifications.db
The SQLite history, created with mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/notify-center/status.json
Unread and total counts, updated after each drain.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/notify-center/spool/
One JSON file per captured notification, removed once processed.
.TP
.I ~/.config/notify-center/config.json
Retention, filtering and display settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify-center-viewer (1)
.PP
The project home page:
.UR https://github.com/jt-at-home/notify-center
.UE
